%% DOCURA - Diagram 17 - Form Session State Machine
%% What the extension is permitted to do in each state.
%% Derived from: FR-EXT-003 to 007, FR-FRM-006/007, FR-SUB-001 to 004, BR-008, BR-014, EC-014 to EC-018
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> Dormant

    state Dormant {
        [*] --> NotReading
        NotReading : Reads nothing. Logs nothing.
        NotReading : Transmits nothing. No indicator.
    }
    note right of Dormant
        BR-014 — there is no passive or
        background observation. Dormant is
        the state on EVERY page until the
        user activates DOCURA on that page.
    end note

    Dormant --> Activated : USER activates DOCURA on this page
    Activated --> Dormant : USER navigates away or closes the page

    state Activated {
        [*] --> Detecting
        Detecting --> NoFormFound : no fillable form on the page
        Detecting --> Interpreting : form detected and fields enumerated
        Interpreting --> Working : meanings and sensitivity tiers assigned
        Working --> Waiting : an ambiguity or approval is outstanding
        Waiting --> Working : USER answers, approves, denies, or skips
        Working --> Remapping : the form changed or fields were added
        Remapping --> Working : stale mappings discarded and the form re-read
        Working --> Reviewing : no fields left to process
        NoFormFound --> Detecting : USER re-activates after the page changes
    }

    Activated --> Stopped : USER stops DOCURA
    Activated --> Degraded : network loss mid-session — EC-014
    Activated --> Expired : session expires mid-form — EC-016
    Activated --> Abandoned : USER submits while DOCURA is mid-action — EC-018

    Degraded --> Activated : USER explicitly resumes
    Expired --> Activated : USER re-authenticates, then re-activates

    Stopped : All activity ceases at once.
    Stopped : Values already placed REMAIN.
    Stopped : Nothing is reverted or cleaned up.
    Stopped : No resume without a FRESH activation.

    Degraded : Initiates no new actions.
    Degraded : Preserves everything already placed.
    Degraded : Shows a clear degraded state.
    Degraded : Never leaves a field half-filled.

    Expired : Halts all automated action immediately.
    Expired : Nothing is filled from a stale session.

    Abandoned : Pending action is abandoned,
    Abandoned : never applied to a submitted form.

    Activated --> HandedBack : review complete
    HandedBack : DOCURA STOPS — BR-008.
    HandedBack : It states that submission is the user's.
    HandedBack : It never operates the submit control.
    HandedBack : Hand-back is recorded; whether the user
    HandedBack : submitted is NOT claimed either way.

    HandedBack --> [*] : USER SUBMITS
    Stopped --> [*]
    Abandoned --> [*]
